        "original_id": "9275ef89-7571-53ed-a990-21b5bceab973",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: University of Virginia, Massachusetts Institute of Technology, U.S. Navy\n- Places: Commonwealth of Virginia, Cambridge, Massachusetts\n- People: Donny Green\n- Systems: Whirlwind I\n- Organizations/Projects: MIT Servomechanisms Laboratory\n- Topics: research universities, college football, Cold War computing\n\nFacts:\n- The University of Virginia, also called U.Va., UVA, or simply Virginia, is a public research university and the flagship university for the Commonwealth of Virginia.\n- The Massachusetts Institute of Technology is a private research university in Cambridge, Massachusetts.\n- Whirlwind I was a Cold War-era vacuum tube computer developed by the MIT Servomechanisms Laboratory for the U.S. Navy.\n- Donny Green played college football at the University of Virginia.\n- Donny Green played for the Washington Redskins and the Jacksonville Jaguars.",
